FAIL

Interpretation:
- FAIL   TestFxReproCopyStringLosesLiveOwnerBehindFourStaleSlots: with four
  stale (finished) owners and one live owner on the same key, MayContain still
  reports a hit, but Lookup's four-entry candidate window is filled with the
  stale slots; validation drops all four and the live owner's taint is lost,
  so propagation.CopyString publishes the copy UNTAINTED (false negative).
- PASS   TestFxControlOneStaleOneLiveIsPreserved: below the cap (1 stale +
  1 live) the live owner's taint survives, matching the authors' contract test
  TestPublishHelpersDropStaleAndPreserveLiveOwner.
- PASS   TestFxControlSequentialChurnReclaimsStaleSlots: four owners that all
  finish and a NEW owner adopting the same address get their dead slots
  reclaimed by putWindow; the new live owner's taint survives. Sequential
  churn cannot construct the failing state: it needs five owners holding
  slots on one address simultaneously.
